  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\nLogic: **Third number = (First number + Second number) + 5**\n\n**(45, 23, 73)**\n\n→ 73 = (45 + 23) + 5\n\n→ 73 = 68 + 5\n\n**(19, 27, 51)**\n\n→ 51 = (19 + 27) + 5\n\n→ 51 = 46 + 5\n\nNow, let's check each option,\n\n1) **(22, 29, 52) **\n\n→ 52 = (22 + 29) + 5\n\n→ 52 ≠ 51 + 5\n\n2) **(12, 19, 30)**\n\n→ 30 = (12 + 19) + 5\n\n→ 30 ≠ 31 + 5\n\n3) **(16, 14, 35)**\n\n→ 35 = (16 + 14) + 5\n\n→ 35 = 30 + 5 ⇒ **Follows the logic.**\n\n4) **(31, 17, 48) **\n\n→ 48 = (31 + 17) + 5\n\n→ 48 ≠ 48 + 5\n\nHere, we can see that only Option 3 follows the logic.\n\nHence, the correct answer is **\"(16, 14, 35)\"**.",
